 ## How it works
-**Inputs and Outputs:**
-The method takes a scalar noise function (typically Perlin or Simplex noise) and a position $\mathbf{p}$ as input. The output is a 3D vector $\mathbf{v}$ representing the velocity at that position. The noise function requires a `seed` and `repeat` parameters for periodicity [S1, unofficial].
